+# Aegis Multimodal Starter (images, audio, video)
+
+This directory contains starter microservices, training scaffolds and CI/cron jobs to enable multimodal support.
+
+Quick overview:
+- services/multimodal/preprocess/* : image/audio/video preprocessing FastAPI services
+- services/multimodal/encoders/clip_finetune.py : CLIP-like finetune script (Hugging Face)
+- k8s/triton/clip-deployment.yaml : Triton deployment example to host image encoder backends
+- tekton/* : Tekton task & pipeline to run multimodal finetune
+- tests/multimodal/* : adversarial suite for images
+- monitoring/cronjobs/* : drift cronjob example
+- services/multimodal/drift/* : embedding drift detector
+
+Getting started (local/dev):
+1. Start preprocess services:
+   - python -m uvicorn services.multimodal.preprocess.image_service:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8081
+   - python -m uvicorn services.multimodal.preprocess.audio_service:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8082
+   - python -m uvicorn services.multimodal.preprocess.video_service:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8083
+
+2. Prepare manifests (ops/multimodal/sample_*_manifest.jsonl) and validate:
+   - python services/multimodal/manifest_uploader.py --manifest ops/multimodal/sample_image_manifest.jsonl
+
+3. Run finetune (small test):
+   - python services/multimodal/encoders/clip_finetune.py --manifest ops/multimodal/sample_image_manifest.jsonl --out_dir out/candidate --epochs 1
+
+4. Run adversarial suite against your model endpoint:
+   - python tests/multimodal/adversarial_image_suite.py
+
+See individual files for configuration and environment variables.
